Named contexts in `~/.config/zenctl/config.toml`. Filesystem only — no bus,
and `ZENKEY_EXPLORER_CONFIG_DIR` is what keeps this corpus out of yours.

```console
$ zenctl context --help
Manage named connection contexts (config file)

Usage: zenctl context <COMMAND>

Commands:
  create  Create (or update) a named context
  list    List contexts (the `*` marks the current one)
  show    Show one context (default: the current one)
  select  Select the current context
  rm      Remove a context
  edit    Open the whole config file in $VISUAL/$EDITOR, validating afterwards
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ zenctl context create --help
Create (or update) a named context

Usage: zenctl context create [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>  

Options:
      --base <BASE>          The deployment base this context pins
  -c, --connect <CONNECT>    Endpoint to connect to, repeatable
  -l, --listen <LISTEN>      Endpoint to listen on, repeatable
      --registry <DIR>       Registry dir, repeatable (offline slice source)
      --scouting             Enable multicast scouting for this context
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>    Default reply timeout in seconds
      --zenoh-config <FILE>  Zenoh JSON5 config file for this context (#122) — the passthrough that reaches a secured bus; explorer knobs apply on top (flag > env > context > file)
      --select               Select it as the current context
  -h, --help                 Print help

$ zenctl context list --help
List contexts (the `*` marks the current one)

Usage: zenctl context list

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ zenctl context show --help
Show one context (default: the current one)

Usage: zenctl context show [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ zenctl context select --help
Select the current context

Usage: zenctl context select <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>  

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ zenctl context rm --help
Remove a context

Usage: zenctl context rm <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>  

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ zenctl context edit --help
Open the whole config file in $VISUAL/$EDITOR, validating afterwards

Usage: zenctl context edit

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

```
